— 🇫🇷 BREAKING: The town hall in Limoges has been set on fire amid ongoing unrest in France.

Rioters are reportedly responsible for the blaze.

@interbellumnews

⚡️🇮🇹Clashes in Bologna in front of the station during a protest against the high cost of living. 

Groups of hooded young people threw stones, bottles, and barriers at the police, who responded with water cannons and tear gas. Dozens of rental bicycles were overturned, and at least seven people were detained.

@medmannews

⚡️🇮🇹Violent clashes in Milan, in Piazza Duomo and Piazza dei Mercanti, where groups of hooded protesters threw stones, bottles, and other objects at the police.

Officers responded with tear gas, charges, and water cannons, dispersing the crowd and clearing the square in front of the cathedral. Several people, including some police officers, were injured and treated by ambulances.

@medmannews

🇫🇷⚡️ I saw a white guy with a French flag in the street, I had to pinch myself to believe it.
In leftist unrest, patriots might as well be unicorns

